# Restrict Meson's built-in `clang-format`/`clang-format-check` targets
# (https://mesonbuild.com/Code-formatting.html) to our own source trees.
#
# Without this file the default pattern is `**/*`, which walks the entire
# source tree including subprojects/ (third-party vendored sources such as
# SDL3, libpng, zlib-ng, mimalloc, etc. - pulled in via wrap files, not ours
# to reformat). That previously reformatted vendored headers in place and
# silently broke them by reordering #include directives that upstream
# projects rely on being in a specific order (e.g. SDL3's
# src/video/khronos/vulkan/vulkan.h including <xcb/xcb.h> before its own
# vulkan_xcb.h, or libpng's pngpriv.h including pngstruct.h before
# pnginfo.h) - clang-format does not treat #include ordering as
# semantically meaningful the way these files need it to be.
Minecraft.Client/**/*
Minecraft.World/**/*
